  "reason": "The exact logarithmic rigidity theorem requires a fixed-slope residual periodically approximable in density, or the additional summable prime-tail condition. Density-zero strict decreases alone do not establish either premise. The absolute-o1 lifting lemma is a sufficient bridge with no proof that the original assumptions yield it. Ordinary additivity and arbitrary finite higher-prime-power values are correctly preserved; the boundary examples fail the density-zero hypothesis or are scalar controls, so none is a full counterexample. Variance-normalized approximations cannot be substituted for the missing absolute-scale implication.",
